1
00:01:27,100 --> 00:01:29,900
Thank you.

2
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:50,900
Assalamu alaikum.

3
00:02:13,900 --> 00:02:18,340
How are you?

4
00:02:18,340 --> 00:02:20,380
Alhamdulillah.

5
00:02:56,880 --> 00:03:03,440
Our book is Ad-Da'u wa al-Dawa' that describes also rifa' to us.

6
00:03:09,780 --> 00:03:16,140
Ad-Da'u wa al-Dawa' was compiled by Al-Imam Ibn al-Qayyim,

7
00:03:16,140 --> 00:03:23,980
as a response to someone who had asked him a question.

8
00:03:25,500 --> 00:03:32,740
This man had approached the Imam, he expressed his condition to the Imam,

9
00:03:32,740 --> 00:03:39,160
he sought a response for what he was in,

10
00:03:39,540 --> 00:03:48,540
because it became so clear that this individual was in a big, big trouble.

11
00:03:49,960 --> 00:03:57,840
He said, the Imam mentioned what this individual said,

12
00:04:09,700 --> 00:04:18,220
What is it that the leading scholars,

13
00:04:19,220 --> 00:04:21,020
What have they said?

14
00:04:22,080 --> 00:04:25,960
The leaders upon the path of the Deen, the scholars,

15
00:04:28,600 --> 00:04:29,200
He said,

16
00:04:34,900 --> 00:04:40,880
What have the heads, the leading scholars amongst the ulama,

17
00:04:40,880 --> 00:04:46,060
What have they said regarding a man,

18
00:04:47,060 --> 00:04:53,880
He was afflicted by a trial, by an affliction,

19
00:05:03,580 --> 00:05:07,820
And this individual clearly knows for certainty,

20
00:05:12,000 --> 00:05:17,240
That if that trouble and affliction continues with him,

21
00:05:18,140 --> 00:05:19,780
This affliction,

22
00:05:23,040 --> 00:05:29,040
It will destroy his dunya, it will destroy his akhirah.

23
00:05:29,960 --> 00:05:34,780
The man understood, if I continue like this,

24
00:05:34,780 --> 00:05:36,900
Life will be bad.

25
00:05:45,720 --> 00:05:52,760
And this man had made a lot of efforts to put away this evil,

26
00:05:53,040 --> 00:05:55,560
this bad behaviour, this bad character,

27
00:05:56,440 --> 00:06:00,860
this sinful life of unrighteousness that he fell into.

28
00:06:00,860 --> 00:06:07,280
He had tried to put it away by all means that he knew.

29
00:06:11,880 --> 00:06:16,240
But as he tried the efforts that he knew,

30
00:06:18,280 --> 00:06:18,360
This thing,

31
00:06:21,900 --> 00:06:26,880
This baliyah was increasing, the affliction, it was worsening,

32
00:06:26,880 --> 00:06:29,080
It got worsened,

33
00:06:29,620 --> 00:06:31,620
in its intensity,

34
00:06:33,140 --> 00:06:34,640
and strength.

35
00:06:40,640 --> 00:06:46,520
What is the way out to put this matter away from myself?

36
00:06:49,680 --> 00:06:52,320
What is the path that I will follow,

37
00:06:53,140 --> 00:06:57,220
so that I can remove this evil from myself?

38
00:07:02,060 --> 00:07:10,040
May Allah shower his mercy and compassion upon whomever becomes merciful,

39
00:07:11,420 --> 00:07:15,260
and provides support to a person that is in an affliction.

40
00:07:16,200 --> 00:07:19,780
Then he cited the hadith to encourage the Prophet Muhammad,

41
00:07:20,520 --> 00:07:26,020
to encourage us, he cited the hadith of the Prophet Muhammad,

42
00:07:26,180 --> 00:07:31,320
so that the scholar is encouraged to answer.

43
00:07:32,660 --> 00:07:36,520
It was not like many do these days.

44
00:07:37,500 --> 00:07:40,200
They want to bully ustaz to answer.

45
00:07:40,960 --> 00:07:42,960
They want to bully sheikh to answer.

46
00:07:43,920 --> 00:07:45,900
So they began to agitate, no.

47
00:07:45,900 --> 00:07:50,480
Encourage him to answer, he may have a lot of issues grappling with.

48
00:07:51,880 --> 00:07:54,240
So he reminded the sheikh,

49
00:07:58,760 --> 00:08:05,200
Sheikh, the way you support,

50
00:08:09,060 --> 00:08:12,100
and will provide support to a servant,

51
00:08:15,900 --> 00:08:24,260
for as long as the servant is upon providing help and support to his brother.

52
00:08:25,020 --> 00:08:25,860
Sheikh, help me.

53
00:08:26,540 --> 00:08:31,140
If you help me and support me, Allah will help you and support you.

54
00:08:33,060 --> 00:08:38,580
Please grant me, provide me the religious willing on this matter.

55
00:08:39,480 --> 00:08:43,940
And as you do so, may Allah reward you abundantly.

56
00:08:47,040 --> 00:08:52,180
May Allah be pleased and show his compassion towards you.

57
00:08:54,220 --> 00:08:56,180
May Allah be pleased with you.

58
00:09:00,200 --> 00:09:06,020
May Allah make us all and you the Imam that I am asking this question.

59
00:09:06,900 --> 00:09:12,080
May Allah grant us ends that are of benefit and goodness to us.

60
00:09:12,440 --> 00:09:13,540
This was his question.

61
00:09:13,540 --> 00:09:15,740
He was in trouble, he was in a worry.

62
00:09:16,920 --> 00:09:21,040
Some of the scholars said he was in a trouble of regularly committing zina.

63
00:09:21,160 --> 00:09:26,300
Some say it was pornography, some say different things the scholars have mentioned.

64
00:09:27,320 --> 00:09:34,840
What the man said regarding himself was he was in an addictive trouble on righteousness.

65
00:09:35,420 --> 00:09:38,480
And that will bring destruction.

66
00:09:38,820 --> 00:09:42,560
No doubt, may Allah protect all of us.

67
00:09:42,560 --> 00:09:51,980
So the Imam Rahimullah Ibn al-Qayyim began to assure him that Allah will bring you out of this condition.

68
00:09:53,320 --> 00:09:59,120
Many times people get into conditions, they become confused, they become worried.

69
00:09:59,880 --> 00:10:10,460
So sometimes the first thing to straighten up in them is that they should be hopeful that Allah will remove them from this evil.

70
00:10:10,460 --> 00:10:24,360
This hope, that Allah will remove me and begin to make efforts to get out of this trouble in the ways that the ulema will suggest.

71
00:10:24,860 --> 00:10:34,840
And we have been reading in this book that is from the aspects of Husnu Zonni Billah, Allah will help me.

72
00:10:34,840 --> 00:10:39,240
Allah will provide support for me out of his mercy.

73
00:10:39,240 --> 00:10:45,960
So I will begin the process of tawbah, all what he had done in the past.

74
00:10:46,580 --> 00:10:53,780
If the tawbah is genuine, if the tawbah is sincere, Allah will provide me help.

75
00:10:54,300 --> 00:10:57,560
He will pardon me if I repent genuinely.

76
00:10:58,660 --> 00:11:08,280
Unfortunately, some of the people continue to remain up on sin, thinking that they are hoping positively in Allah.

77
00:11:08,280 --> 00:11:24,580
If the hope with Allah is positive, then we must begin to take steps out of sin, if your hope, if your anticipation of goodness with Allah is genuine.

78
00:11:25,960 --> 00:11:32,380
That is known by the individuals taking steps out of the old ways.

79
00:11:32,380 --> 00:11:35,800
Imam Ibn al-Qayyim said,

80
00:11:41,720 --> 00:11:55,060
There is no doubt that a person is thinking positively, anticipating goodness and beneficence from Allah.

81
00:11:58,860 --> 00:12:04,440
You find it and it actually occurs when you are doing what is right.

82
00:12:05,500 --> 00:12:09,840
If a person is doing what is right, what does he expect? Good rewards.

83
00:12:10,840 --> 00:12:11,160
He said,

84
00:12:19,900 --> 00:12:24,660
Because this one who is thinking and hoping for goodness from Allah.

85
00:12:25,260 --> 00:12:25,920
The Imam said,

86
00:12:29,220 --> 00:12:38,540
He definitely hopes in goodness in Allah, that Allah will give him good rewards, Allah will give me good recompense.

87
00:12:40,480 --> 00:12:42,720
And Allah does not break his promise.

88
00:12:43,540 --> 00:12:48,080
He promises, if you observe Salah, I will be kind to you. If you pay Zakat, I reward you.

89
00:12:48,940 --> 00:12:50,440
You make dua, I will accept.

90
00:12:51,700 --> 00:12:55,560
The one who is not making dua is waiting for goodness. You did not ask for anything.

91
00:12:56,520 --> 00:13:00,660
The one who is up on Zina is hoping for goodness. You are up on sinfulness.

92
00:13:01,660 --> 00:13:03,160
So the Imam said,

93
00:13:10,300 --> 00:13:20,100
The one who is hoping for goodness is so doing because he anticipates goodness, good rewards for what he has done.

94
00:13:21,240 --> 00:13:21,400
He said,

95
00:13:22,700 --> 00:13:25,440
And Allah does not break his promise.

96
00:13:27,160 --> 00:13:31,780
If I repent and I am repenting, Allah accepts repentance.

97
00:13:32,680 --> 00:13:34,760
And really this thing really comes to mind.

98
00:13:35,560 --> 00:13:40,060
If something happens and the individual regrets, why did I do this?

99
00:13:40,980 --> 00:13:50,460
As you carry on that mindset of regret and never to proceed, it begins to come to your mind that Allah accepts it.

100
00:13:50,460 --> 00:13:56,800
You have one reverse calmness in your mind regarding Tawbah.

101
00:13:58,300 --> 00:13:58,920
So he said,

102
00:13:59,780 --> 00:14:18,520
But as for the one who is al-Musi' is regularly upon evil practices.

103
00:14:20,960 --> 00:14:24,340
He is always upon major sins.

104
00:14:24,480 --> 00:14:27,680
Today he drinks alcohol. Tomorrow he comes to Zina.

105
00:14:27,940 --> 00:14:29,360
Next tomorrow he is up on gambling.

106
00:14:30,060 --> 00:14:34,520
The other day he is up on telling a lie to deceive the people to collect the money from them.

107
00:14:34,840 --> 00:14:37,220
Or zulm, being unjust to people.

108
00:14:38,060 --> 00:14:42,060
Walmukhalafat and other deeds of disobedience to Allah.

109
00:14:44,620 --> 00:14:50,660
Where will he find being positive and anticipating goodness?

110
00:14:51,160 --> 00:14:54,820
Will he even have time to think that Allah will show a mercy upon him?

111
00:14:56,940 --> 00:15:00,360
So Imam al-Hasan al-Basri was cited.

112
00:15:01,060 --> 00:15:04,600
Ibn al-Qayyim cited Imam al-Hasan al-Basri who said,

113
00:15:12,060 --> 00:15:15,340
The people of the person of Iman,

114
00:15:15,340 --> 00:15:20,480
He was hopeful in the mercy of Allah.

115
00:15:20,980 --> 00:15:23,320
He was looking for rewards from Allah.

116
00:15:23,840 --> 00:15:26,120
He was looking for goodness with Allah.

117
00:15:26,740 --> 00:15:30,820
He was looking for tranquility and good mind from Allah.

118
00:15:30,900 --> 00:15:33,080
Allah grant me this. Allah grant me this.

119
00:15:35,240 --> 00:15:38,700
That Mu'min, he therefore made his deeds to be good.

120
00:15:38,700 --> 00:15:42,380
I want good from Allah. Let me use good deeds.

121
00:15:43,640 --> 00:15:46,460
I want protection from Allah. Let me make Salat.

122
00:15:47,740 --> 00:15:51,000
I want progress. I want goodness for my children.

123
00:15:51,140 --> 00:15:53,180
Let me make haste towards that.

124
00:15:55,260 --> 00:15:57,180
The person of Iman,

125
00:16:00,640 --> 00:16:03,240
He hopes for goodness from his Lord.

126
00:16:05,840 --> 00:16:07,740
So he makes his good to be good.

127
00:16:08,300 --> 00:16:10,440
Why? He is expecting goodness from Allah.

128
00:16:12,880 --> 00:16:14,500
As for the criminal,

129
00:16:17,280 --> 00:16:21,280
He is not thinking. He is thinking about Allah is not positive.

130
00:16:23,400 --> 00:16:25,280
So his deeds are bad.

131
00:16:26,440 --> 00:16:29,300
Bad deeds make you think evil about Allah.

132
00:16:30,040 --> 00:16:33,780
But it would be unfortunate if the individual is upon evil deeds.

133
00:16:34,880 --> 00:16:36,920
He is now expecting good rewards.

134
00:16:37,680 --> 00:16:41,280
Ibn al-Qayyim went to cite about 38 ahadith.

135
00:16:42,220 --> 00:16:47,360
To say that, like he called it, that it is part of al-hamaka.

136
00:16:48,140 --> 00:16:49,920
A person is being stupid.

137
00:16:50,920 --> 00:16:52,560
To be upon evil deeds.

138
00:16:53,240 --> 00:16:54,260
He drinks alcohol.

139
00:16:55,220 --> 00:16:56,200
He gambles.

140
00:16:57,140 --> 00:16:58,300
He is upon riba.

141
00:17:00,120 --> 00:17:01,880
He is upon zina.

142
00:17:02,080 --> 00:17:04,120
He tells lies. He deceives.

143
00:17:05,300 --> 00:17:07,240
He is arrogant towards his parents.

144
00:17:08,800 --> 00:17:12,000
He delays Salah and observes Salah just when he likes.

145
00:17:13,380 --> 00:17:15,720
And he refuses perhaps to observe zakah.

146
00:17:16,420 --> 00:17:18,720
He has the money, he will not go for hajj.

147
00:17:20,800 --> 00:17:22,580
And then in all of these,

148
00:17:23,380 --> 00:17:24,780
when he is encouraged, Mektub says,

149
00:17:25,000 --> 00:17:27,620
No, we are hoping for goodness from Allah.

150
00:17:28,440 --> 00:17:29,440
Upon sinfulness,

151
00:17:30,240 --> 00:17:31,960
the ulamas say this is hamaka.

152
00:17:32,900 --> 00:17:33,880
It is stupidity.

153
00:17:34,520 --> 00:17:35,900
It does not make sense.

154
00:17:36,760 --> 00:17:38,740
It is opposite intelligence.

155
00:17:39,700 --> 00:17:42,900
That the deeds of the prophets call it that.

156
00:17:44,400 --> 00:17:47,960
It refers to such persons as al-ajizu.

157
00:17:49,400 --> 00:17:51,340
He said alayhi salatu was salam.

158
00:17:51,580 --> 00:17:52,840
He said, al-ajiz,

159
00:17:53,300 --> 00:17:57,660
the one who is far from being sensible,

160
00:17:58,640 --> 00:18:02,060
is that person whose deeds are bad.

161
00:18:03,000 --> 00:18:05,500
The prophet said alayhi salatu was salam.

162
00:18:05,920 --> 00:18:07,320
So al-ajiz,

163
00:18:07,920 --> 00:18:12,880
the one whose deeds are far from being sensible,

164
00:18:13,720 --> 00:18:15,180
at all.

165
00:18:16,000 --> 00:18:17,800
The deeds are bad.

166
00:18:18,360 --> 00:18:19,840
He commits sin.

167
00:18:20,040 --> 00:18:22,300
He is not, his deeds are not,

168
00:18:23,060 --> 00:18:25,280
they are not in line with goodness.

169
00:18:28,060 --> 00:18:32,760
He makes his soul to follow just whatever he desires.

170
00:18:34,080 --> 00:18:36,020
Whatever he desires, just do it.

171
00:18:37,660 --> 00:18:39,080
When he follows his desires,

172
00:18:39,560 --> 00:18:41,960
